2026-10-03T12:47:47.7285714Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-03T12:47:47.7295858Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-03T12:47:47.7296590Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-03T12:47:47.7297342Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-03T12:47:47.7298006Z 
2026-10-03T12:47:47.7298311Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-03T12:47:47.7298778Z 
2026-10-03T12:47:47.7299124Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-03T12:47:47.7299883Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-03T12:47:47.7300291Z 
2026-10-03T12:47:47.7300485Z If you would like to
2026-10-03T12:47:47.7300889Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-03T12:47:47.7301078Z 
2026-10-03T12:47:47.7301308Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-03T12:47:47.7301683Z   $ sh ./install-nix
